---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  lang="en"
  title="Model card · SketchSense"
  description="SketchSense browser CNN evidence and limitations."
>
  <main class="container document-page">
    <a href={`${base}en/`}>← Back to SketchSense</a><h1>Model card</h1><p>
      Sketch-cnn-v3 classifies drawings across 16 Quick, Draw! categories. It
      runs locally in the browser, never transmits the drawing, and abstains on
      weak evidence.
    </p><h2>Measured evaluation</h2><p>
      On the held-out 8,000-drawing vector test: 94.63% accuracy, 94.61% macro
      F1, 98.76% top-3 accuracy, and 79.8% worst-class recall.
    </p><h2>Architecture and artifact</h2><p>
      Two batch-normalized convolution blocks and a two-layer classifier contain
      422,608 parameters. The fixed-batch ONNX opset 18 artifact is 1,707,724
      bytes and outputs 16 logits from a 28 × 28 input.
    </p><h2>Limitations</h2><p>
      Only 16 categories are supported. Ambiguous, unusual, faint, or
      out-of-distribution sketches may still be wrong. Confidence is a model
      score rather than a guarantee, even when the interface does not abstain.
      The model is an educational portfolio demonstration, not a safety-critical
      classifier.
    </p><p>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/SebastianGaray/sketchsense/blob/main/docs/model-card.md"
        >Full reproducibility record on GitHub</a
      >
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
